## Scope Contract 2: Integrate Semantic Validation

**Objective**: Add semantic product validation to product fetch with console logging.

**Files to Modify**:
- `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` - Add semantic wrapper
- `app/(store)/products/[...category]/page.tsx` - Add console logging

**Files to Create**:
- `lib/catalogue/semanticLogger.ts` - Console formatting utilities

**DoD - Layer 1 (Structure)**:
- [ ] New function `getSelectedProductsWithValidation()` wraps existing function
- [ ] Returns same shape as original (products, totalProductsCount)
- [ ] Semantic analysis runs on returned products array
- [ ] Logger utility with `logSemanticSummary()` and `logSemanticDetails()` functions

**DoD - Layer 2 (Layout)**:
- [ ] Validation runs after product fetch (non-blocking to return)
- [ ] Summary statistics calculated: valid (>=80), moderate (60-79), invalid (<60)
- [ ] Console header format: "=== Category: [Name] | [X] products ==="
- [ ] Per-product log format: "[emoji] [Product Name] ([score]/100)"
- [ ] Summary line: "Valid: X | Moderate: Y | Invalid: Z | Avg: Z%"

**DoD - Layer 3 (Surface)**:
- [ ] Emojis: ✅ (>=80), ⚠️ (60-79), ❌ (<60)
- [ ] Product names truncated at 40 chars with "..."
- [ ] Category context included
- [ ] Score color coding in console (if supported)
- [ ] Empty category shows: "⚠️ No products in category"

**DoD - Layer 4 (Interaction)**:
- [ ] Only runs when `process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development'`
- [ ] Errors in validation caught and logged, don't break fetch
- [ ] Large product lists (>20) show summary only, not individual products
- [ ] Feature flag: `DISABLE_SEMANTIC_LOGS` to disable
- [ ] Performance: <5ms overhead

**Verification (Testing)**:
- [ ] Unit test: Returns same products as original function
- [ ] Unit test: Semantic scores calculated correctly for known products
- [ ] Unit test: Console output formatted correctly
- [ ] E2E test: /products/headphones/open-back shows semantic logs
- [ ] E2E test: /products/audio-electronics/desktop-amps shows semantic logs
- [ ] E2E test: Production build has no semantic logs

---

