## Sprint Execution Sequence

**Phase 1: Foundation & Safety (Day 1)**
1. Write regression tests (Scope Contract 5, Layers 1-2)
2. Fix DetailSection.tsx `<a>` → `Link` (Scope Contract 1, all layers)
3. Run E2E tests - verify navigation works
4. Test all 22 category navigation paths manually

**Phase 2: Semantic Validation (Day 2)**
5. Create semanticLogger.ts utility (Scope Contract 2, Layers 1-2)
6. Integrate into getSelectedProducts.ts (Scope Contract 2, Layers 3-4)
7. Add logging to [...category]/page.tsx
8. Verify console output shows semantic matches

**Phase 3: Polish (Day 3)**
9. Fix SidebarClient.tsx colors (Scope Contract 3)
10. Fix getCatalogueData.ts console.log (Scope Contract 4)
11. Run visual regression tests
12. Full regression test run

**Phase 4: Verification (Day 4)**
13. Test all 22 category pages for semantic matches
14. Verify console logging output
15. Final regression test suite
16. Performance benchmark (navigation should be faster with Link)

---

## Success Criteria

**Functional**:
- [ ] Clicking catalogue item uses client-side navigation (no page reload)
- [ ] All 22 category paths navigate correctly
- [ ] Console shows semantic match scores for products
- [ ] Products displayed match category semantically (>=80 score ideally)
- [ ] No hardcoded colors in SidebarClient
- [ ] No console.log in production build

**Performance**:
- [ ] Navigation time <100ms (was ~500-1000ms with full reload)
- [ ] Semantic validation overhead <5ms
- [ ] Lighthouse score improved (client-side nav)

**Quality**:
- [ ] All regression tests pass
- [ ] All E2E tests pass
- [ ] No TypeScript errors
- [ ] No ESLint warnings
- [ ] No console errors

---

## Rollback Plan

If navigation breaks:
1. Revert DetailSection.tsx to `<a>` temporarily
2. Debug Link implementation
3. Re-apply fix

